{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{% block body %}
{% include '_processing_banner.html.twig' %}
<style>
.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px;margin:0}.pair img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;border-radius:4px;background:#e6e6dd}.pair figcaption{grid-column:1/-1;font-size:.78rem;color:#6c756a;line-height:1.5}
.label{font-size:.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#6c756a;margin:6px 0 0}
.stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:16px;border-top:1px solid #d7d4cb;border-bottom:1px solid #d7d4cb;padding:20px 0;margin:8px 0 12px}.stats b{display:block;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:2.2rem;font-weight:400}.stats span{font-size:.8rem;color:#6c756a}
.flow{list-style:none;padding:0;counter-reset:step;display:grid;gap:14px}.flow li{counter-increment:step;display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.2rem 1fr;gap:4px 12px}.flow li::before{content:counter(step);grid-row:span 2;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:1.6rem;color:#345c49}.flow strong{font-weight:600}.flow p{margin:0;font-size:.93rem;line-height:1.55}
@media(max-width:700px){.stats{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}}
</style>
<section class="hero">
    <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Symfony AI &amp; MCP Hackathon entry</span>
        <h1>Gravestone photos in, searchable records out.</h1>
        <p>MemorialAtlas reads phone photos of grave markers. For each marker it proposes a record: the names, the dates and the inscription, with what is still uncertain.</p>
        <p>A person checks every record against the photo. The photo stays the evidence.</p>
        <p><a class="button" href="{{ path('item_search') }}">Search the collection</a> &nbsp; <a href="#how">How it works ↓</a></p>
    </div>
    {% if heroImage %}{% set cleaned = memorial_cleaned(heroImage) %}
    {% if cleaned %}
    <figure class="pair">
        <div><img src="{{ memorial_detail(heroImage) }}" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" alt="Original phone photo of a gravestone, taken at an angle"><p class="label">Phone photo</p></div>
        <div><img src="{{ cleaned }}" loading="eager" alt="The same gravestone, straightened and relit by an image model"><p class="label">AI-cleaned view</p></div>
        <figcaption>Taken on a cold, windy afternoon. Jev judged the photo angled, and Gemini made a straightened copy for display. OCR and extraction read only the original. <a href="{{ path('item_show', {id: heroImage.item.id}) }}">See this record →</a></figcaption>
    </figure>
    {% else %}
    <figure><img src="{{ memorial_detail(heroImage) }}" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" alt="A gravestone from the collection"><figcaption>Every record begins with a photograph. <a href="{{ path('item_show', {id: heroImage.item.id}) }}">See this record →</a></figcaption></figure>
    {% endif %}{% endif %}
</section>

<section style="max-width:860px">
<h2>The collection</h2>
<p>{{ stats.photos }} photos of headstones in St. Peter's churchyard, Virginia, taken in about half an hour on 13 November 2026, while a drone flew over the same graves. The photos are public on <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/museado/memorialatlas-st-peters">Hugging Face</a>, so anyone can run the same pipeline on them.</p>
<div class="stats">
    <div><b>{{ stats.photos }}</b><span>photos</span></div>
    <div><b>{{ stats.withOcr }}</b><span>read by OCR</span></div>
    <div><b>{{ stats.records }}</b><span>records ready to review</span></div>
    <div><b>{{ stats.cleaned }}</b><span>AI-cleaned views</span></div>
</div>
<p class="muted" style="font-size:.85rem">Counts come from the database when the page loads. The view from the drone is on the <a href="{{ path('drone') }}">Drone page</a>.</p>

<h2 id="how">What happens to each photo</h2>
<ol class="flow">
    <li><strong>Read the inscription.</strong><p>Mistral OCR reads the text on the stone.</p></li>
    <li><strong>Decide what the photo needs.</strong><p>Jev, a TypeSafe decision model, answers fixed questions with probabilities: is this a gravestone, is the OCR usable, how many people does it name, was the camera at an angle. The answers choose the next steps, so a clear photo costs less than a hard one.</p></li>
    <li><strong>Look at the stone.</strong><p>When the OCR is weak, Mistral Medium describes the photo itself: the layout, the symbols, the letters OCR missed.</p></li>
    <li><strong>Propose a record.</strong><p>Mistral turns the evidence into structured data, validated into a PHP object: title, people with birth and death dates, and a list of what is uncertain. A shared surname is not proof of family, and a name on a stone is not proof of burial.</p></li>
    <li><strong>Clean up angled photos.</strong><p>If Jev judges the photo angled, Gemini makes a straightened, evenly lit copy for display. An image model can change letters, so the copy is labelled and never read by OCR or extraction.</p></li>
    <li><strong>Search it, or ask about it.</strong><p>Records go into Elasticsearch for search, a public read-only API, and an MCP server, so an AI assistant can search the collection and quote a record with its open questions.</p></li>
</ol>

<h2>Built with Symfony AI and MCP</h2>
<p>Each model is a Symfony AI platform bridge (Mistral, Gemini, TypeSafe), so switching a provider is a configuration change. Structured output maps model answers to typed PHP classes. A Messenger worker runs the pipeline, and every AI answer is stored with its model, prompt and input hash, so a record shows where each reading came from. The MCP server uses <code>symfony/mcp-bundle</code> and the PHP MCP SDK, with tools declared by attributes. <a href="{{ path('about') }}">More about the technology →</a></p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
